WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.556
- [Narrator] In Kassel, Germany,

00:00:01.556 --> 00:00:02.990
for a limited time only,

00:00:02.990 --> 00:00:03.823
there is a replica

00:00:03.823 --> 00:00:04.901
of the Greek structure,

00:00:04.901 --> 00:00:06.519
The Parthenon, and it's made

00:00:06.519 --> 00:00:08.948
with over 100,000 banned books.

00:00:08.948 --> 00:00:11.531
(upbeat music)

00:00:15.135 --> 00:00:16.255
The ‘Parthenon of Books’

00:00:16.255 --> 00:00:17.458
is an installation that

00:00:17.458 --> 00:00:20.717
is part of The Document of 14 art show.

00:00:20.717 --> 00:00:21.858
The exhibit is from

00:00:21.858 --> 00:00:24.193
South American artist, Martin Minujín.

00:00:24.193 --> 00:00:26.273
Her aim is to spark debate

00:00:26.273 --> 00:00:29.130
about the issues of
censorship in literature.

00:00:29.130 --> 00:00:31.062
To achieve that, she has collected

00:00:31.062 --> 00:00:33.645
over a hundred thousand copies of 170

00:00:33.645 --> 00:00:34.549
different books that

00:00:34.549 --> 00:00:35.481
have been banned

00:00:35.481 --> 00:00:36.523
throughout the world

00:00:36.523 --> 00:00:38.304
through various stages of history.

00:00:38.304 --> 00:00:39.813
The books include everything

00:00:39.813 --> 00:00:42.019
from Mark Twain's Adventures of Tom Sawyer

00:00:42.019 --> 00:00:43.889
to Cecily von Ziegesar's Gossip Girl.

00:00:43.889 --> 00:00:46.677
It is not a coincidence that The Parthenon

00:00:46.677 --> 00:00:49.114
of Books is located in this German park

00:00:49.114 --> 00:00:51.301
as it was here that Nazi’s burned

00:00:51.301 --> 00:00:53.948
over 2,000 books by
Jewish or Marxist writers

00:00:53.948 --> 00:00:55.500
in the early 1930s.

00:00:55.500 --> 00:00:57.040
The books for this project

00:00:57.040 --> 00:00:58.810
were donated by the general public.

00:00:58.810 --> 00:01:00.885
And once the installation is complete,

00:01:00.885 --> 00:01:02.794
they will be handed out to visitors

00:01:02.794 --> 00:01:04.242
with the hope of inspiring readers

00:01:04.242 --> 00:01:05.290
for years to come.

00:01:05.290 --> 00:01:07.873
(upbeat music)

